Washington Spirit v Kansas City Current: where the NWSL Championship will b=
e won and lost


Croix Bethune, Trinity Rodman and the Rowdy Audi crowd are among the factor=
s that could swing Saturday=E2=80=99s final


Trinity Rodman and her Washington Spirit teammates Esme Morgan and Melissa =
Bethi celebrate scoring against Portland Thorns. Photograph: Hannah Foslien=
/NWSL/Getty Images


Megan Swanick


This year=E2=80=99s NWSL Championship blends recurring themes with some new=
ness. For the familiar: the Washington Spirit are in the final for the thir=
d straight year, hoping the third time=E2=80=99s the charm after back-to-ba=
ck 1-0 defeats in their past two attempts. Slightly familiar, too, is Kansa=
s City Current playing the championship game at Washington=E2=80=99s Audi F=
ield, where they lost the final to Portland in 2022 and where they will con=
tend again Saturday.

For the novelty? Neither Kansas City nor Washington, despite their modern d=
ominance in the NWSL table, have won the championship since 2021 (when Wash=
ington won). With Gotham=E2=80=99s bid for a two-peat
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
