leaving
Washington for Missouri in February, Bethune is facing her former team for =
the chance to win her first championship trophy.

A bit more poetry: Bethune
nearly
broke the NWSL=E2=80=99s all-time single-season assists record during her 2=
024 rookie season for the Spirit. (A torn meniscus cut short her streak, bu=
t she still was named Rookie of the Year.) She finally broke it this season=
 with Kansas City. Her creative influence in the Current=E2=80=99s midfield=
 has been crucial to unlocking their goal-scoring capabilities. Bethune=E2=
=80=99s ability to pull apart Washington=E2=80=99s laudable defensive struc=
ture could prove crucial in the final.


Kansas City Current star Croix Bethune was named this season=E2=80=99s Midf=
ielder of the Year. Photograph: William Purnell/Imagn Images/Reuters


Kansas City=E2=80=99s attacking depth
Temwa Chawinga is a two-time NWSL MVP for a reason, but she wasn=E2=80=99t =
the sole source of Kansas City=E2=80=99s 54 goals in 30 regular season game=
s. The Current=E2=80=99s past nine goals (across five games including the p=
layoffs) were scored by six different players, with Haley Hopkins (tied wit=
h Chawinga for goal contributions in the regular season) notching four of t=
hem. Chawinga enters the Championship with only one goal contribution in fi=
ve games and no goals since 3 October, but she can break through at any mom=
ent. If not, the Current=E2=80=99s surrounding cast of contributors =E2=80=
=93 Hopkins, Michelle Cooper, Bethune and Debinha =E2=80=93 seems prepared =
to make the difference.


Temwa Chawinga could be due for a breakout game in Saturday=E2=80=99s final=
. Photograph: Ira L Black/Getty Images


Rodman is the Spirit=E2=80=99s gamechanger
The Spirit also have attacking depth, but Rodman is a gamechanger whose imp=
act is more lopsided. Her 20 goal contributions in the regular season were =
more than double the goal contributions of any teammate, and that=E2=80=99s=
 without quantifying the space she frees up for fellow goalscorers with her=
 calculated off-the-ball movements.

In the postseason, Rodman has four goal contributions in two games =E2=80=
=93 two goals and two assists. Coming at the end of one of her best club se=
asons, a big performance in the final will be essential for a Spirit victor=
y. It would also further solidify her as one of the deserved main character=
s (and
