<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In as much as any derby can ever be a free=
 hit, there was always a sense that Mauricio Pochettino=E2=80=99s first gam=
e as Manchester United manager wouldn=E2=80=99t matter too much; nobody exp=
ected them to win away to Liverpool. This was not a game on which anybody w=
as going to judge him, and that feeling only magnified when Leny Yoro was s=
ent off after eight minutes. <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardia=
n.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECoBtcQjat6FvTX4oD=
JNDqNGWZ489GMuF8pC0eU0geQE85nP3ked8hBUJamWNB8-EUDqLADwsei1hreX_IP0priEekRs_=
ZGqmvClaVFqWiKeQIq27UTRcP5Y43EIy-8Zpo2fPe4Iz0TOe5dMtZYcjH3FoMR2xcN_UFb2UA47=
tumViI_qJ6oLmM4WCWU13-TOpnPNKa57TggUNX4VocXFswg2j33yhkDKomPJBC1djRhGoBh5q1h=
btRxdKgExpQSWCuU5IRsGTILR0-nu_lDbjdC2v1FAGAY7NlMTfxh1N7r8FSfh0mhSASg6oR09P6=
zbRI/4vz/HHKhgrEVQVWIz4sBnGP78g/h10/h001._3LkwwnCe6ljrFnRcj6fPrvLnyfQ2e_Evr=
XKRlhxU3w" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">United=E2=80=99s victory at Anfield la=
st season</a> was their first for a decade; what=E2=80=99s difficult to do =
with 11 men is only going to get harder playing a man down for 82 minutes. =
But that does not mean that it did not matter.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Although Roy Keane was determined to rejec=
t the suggestion, there was perhaps even some credit to be gleaned from hav=
ing <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEm=
Fuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgrtoJtFn_siZKCp_h9y0z=
_bXqBscx62ydtMlzzM5cd1HvCqkDSf7r0DK6gCJbCXM-chbkjWKZYqmUBUeDAR9wI6S8RExiv55=
9EaZZ9KC1dAOzldevPJDEmIMp6QN12Zeto2VXi_22i6-mLsvF_ZKFSNIvR0CdmoNKnZYMuNtU8i=
qEDFReGt5F1cUco_we-GDcWhAe6urW4DY4SQvnJk_6hmzBBtauNXpcWIRV1kNstqoljicbC6XcR=
hqfw-hIS2fcZPTZIcf4wEg1Hd9Oj8wUdV4t0gPLHPhrQpJNqzL7eI4/4vz/HHKhgrEVQVWIz4sB=
nGP78g/h11/h001.-XIaJNeQlsmVeUgEWlbqEMcSq648e9QhFfZXqZuErb4" style=3D"color=
: #0077B6;">lost only 4-0</a>. Certainly when they were 2-0 down after 13 m=
inutes, there was reason for United to fear an embarrassment akin to their =
<a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuif=
c_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDdU1IxeDnOTgt6YHM8QyEWcxSehHqLuCy4aeLrmL2OkASu=
teVI3XyAE37NLIrf2RMZHjHe3cD-0ihQFUhb6SpNy2OuEYL6XB2qGGLDS6gjH5USTq-7c6dtxsM=
o9jEpJ_E6U0lCNrHt4TP4I91GCClWpAXv4virdPTFnlLlQnibC-Q1K8I_EZ5IXenbQWY7uB71Ug=
TD44ileSgQwePXUltwWR8UaLhRWjxKJijgS2BoFrq624hvn_qu9O0rPiM-_CqQynmTUI7sNtaTs=
WU2Hq88Z7Xs1HyQoPMvuWnGl1rux0Vj5F_3720yGMCpKdjqNns/4vz/HHKhgrEVQVWIz4sBnGP7=
8g/h12/h001.1A8vRi1p_qUyDNjYjrxVFJ4XGS7yduvyRx6xs5zLQA4" style=3D"color: #0=
077B6;">7-0 defeat against Liverpool in 2023</a>. Perhaps Pochettino deserv=
es credit for his switch to a back three, which brought a degree of stabili=
sation, but United could easily have lost far more comfortably than they di=
d. Liverpool had 18 shots in the game three-and-a-half years ago, eight of =
them on target; on Sunday they had 28, 11 of them on target. When you=E2=80=
=99ve conceded an xG of 4.38, there=E2=80=99s not much point quibbling over=
 the details; you=E2=80=99ve been hammered.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">And when you=E2=80=99ve conceded more goal=
s in all competitions this season than anybody else in Europe=E2=80=99s top=
 five leagues, and when you=E2=80=99ve let in more in the league than anybo=
dy other than Crystal Palace, it=E2=80=99s pretty obvious that the defence =
is a major problem. There are serious reasons for concern; a switch of mana=
ger alone will not magically save United.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Perhaps Yoro was unfortunate to be sent of=
f. Senne Lammens may have got to the ball ahead of Alexander Isak. But the =
opposite is also true. Had Yoro not been sent off, it would only have been =
because Isak=E2=80=99s first touch was heavy. By far the bigger issue as Po=
chettino prepares for Wednesday=E2=80=99s Champions League game at Sporting=
 and Saturday=E2=80=99s Premier League match at home to Brentford is how ea=
sily United were undone by a simple ball over the top. First Matthijs de Li=
gt, who was much deeper than the rest of the defensive line, inexcusably le=
ft it, and then Yoro, in scrambling back, made an appallingly clumsy foul.<=
/p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">De Ligt, who has only been back in trainin=
g for six weeks as he recovers from a back injury, had not started a league=
 game since November last year. He looked way off the pace, as he had in th=
e <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFu=
ifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgT0wLr-a4BDJODV0NjT7ZDy=
JiSl5PtrJ5xu-pMe5IZy8MoE3cC5xgsl-tfEVTPRnaQVis1IoHXoSWDiLHj8tTVUXgti9SVDMLj=
wPeyOmxLSJqnvqSwkSIeBf_e-O7JHacXoxgVMdPAbCpTAyacN3aYLCMbOad2jGZu7HmEgErdHO_=
M7lMbtqBqp53T2TFwNhwu5renpl8JGbj3PnbfxZSRu6vmG7Pa0uP5UxC4LY3OhOXknSEecHGg3y=
z-qy_s7Q_WPGDmhnoVWnZk6zyk_6UgA/4vz/HHKhgrEVQVWIz4sBnGP78g/h13/h001.oufsHH-=
Py7Dib6Ofq-AKgGgIwJDf4x7He-ISF-8h_H0" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">defeat to C=
omo</a>, and his selection, in retrospect, was an error by Pochettino. Yoro=
, who had looked one of United=E2=80=99s better recent signings in his firs=
t year after signing from Lille, had become a case study in the damage bein=
g part of a dysfunctional team can do to a player: his confidence is shot a=
nd he now lurches around like a sad horse, a player who seems always to be =
at the centre of unfortunate events =E2=80=93 such as that header against h=
is own bar against Aston Villa.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">There are manifold problems at United, fro=
m the leadership to the recruitment to the stadium, but if there is to be a=
n improvement in form, the first thing Pochettino needs to do is to change =
the mood. This is nothing like a great squad. It is a mess of ideas and str=
ategies, put together over six different managers with no consistent goal i=
n sight. But it is not a squad made up of terrible players. It is a squad m=
ade up of players who have lost their way, who had been dragged down into t=
he morass. It=E2=80=99s obvious that United should be better than this, but=
 even this United should be better than this.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">United have won only one of 11 games in th=
e league this season, and that was <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theg=
uardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYca=
NsDra0BxnPgHYuXnMXQUq8U9bOS0OBrGhlee_vVv15FvYPcmsPNeVuJ5q1tDGSYesU2Qy07qTha=
vsL7oI82SFScV6VT-wgpv00CLk4PWaW9VK4hrhnKwYUyOUapEszB76AK6A6VyEi1hfblDIoLCaS=
RxGGNSz0EmTnIgGxZ4_dju0A9yP-ZXOhemG71A78jbeSDtCRGXtOZC8GwTbvLGHiN8YenLGvITE=
ejT9ppFfV6WC_KYoxBlNp11DzMegGJWWlIegu_9bou3CjBdTIRN7yD8U-u3cgklxNVeHdnlu6Ip=
B7YCmLYMYY/4vz/HHKhgrEVQVWIz4sBnGP78g/h14/h001.difMPKREkb6CY--Bq4ogfqjnaxjO=
Hx4ScZ3ifzfRwAA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">against newly-promoted Ipswich i=
n August</a>. To put that in context, Burnley are the only other side of al=
l 92 in the league not to have won at least twice; when <a href=3D"https://=
ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEM=
gszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPglG-y9vvrogjjt75eIDhkJuOe_JMbbCl5ySPKtagnzHf=
A8qBD2SfGR47KSn9GoSWglCc_1MHT0v6yJHes1KhJcTQSVdiTHYlFDRkn-OYLBBmlyUbmjCYaTk=
0CU0RVciDPRW5H9O4cfBq8dhNcYJP-HbK5nGbIvKaEK8z-dQKlULZJEELmbdedmgHpAVNbOKd2W=
6MAJhcq3_4xTcopXj-Hqbm4XKwcRMbiWuV549R6fbqJqKax_vtBLCUmCf_sS2_L2Z7aNR_qb4xV=
2IK0W0pC12XpBTgpNp2ChDJS1ratNK4/4vz/HHKhgrEVQVWIz4sBnGP78g/h15/h001.a4Kbn1m=
Boe4jRt3Ud0WwgQJnBVqeKy2k0HtsRyRT4aM" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">United were=
 relegated in 1973-74</a>, they won three of their first 11 games. Bruno Fe=
rnades has now played in four defeats to Liverpool by four goals or more, a=
 record.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It remains, still, almost inconceivable th=
at United will be relegated, or even that they will find themselves in a pr=
oper battle. It=E2=80=99s almost a category error; this cannot happen. But =
there are no terrible sides in the Premier League this season. Perhaps Manc=
hester City=E2=80=99s appeal will fail and their punishment means they will=
 obligingly occupy one of the relegation slots. But the three promoted side=
s are all showing signs of fight. Crystal Palace will probably improve unde=
r Thomas Frank, Sunderland have started keeping clean sheets and are a very=
 different side if Brian Brobbey is fit, Nottingham Forest are far better t=
han their league positions suggests and Fulham are five league games unbeat=
en.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">A bounce will, surely, come at some point =
under Pochettino but, this season, nothing can be taken for granted at the =
bottom.</p>
