<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>By Jeff Rueter</strong></p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The MLS Cup Playoffs kicked off in earnest=
 over the weekend, with the higher seeds hosting the first match of their b=
est-of-three series. These days, the domestic league has fewer members of t=
he perceived US =E2=80=9CA-team=E2=80=9D than ever. Instead, its direct imp=
act on the senior national team mostly sorts into two categories: players w=
ho have perfected specific roles with their clubs that could boost the nati=
onal team, and as a bountiful talent development pipeline.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The past two windows ushered in much of th=
e next generation. This group of players, headlined by <em><strong style=3D=
"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Cavan Sullivan</str=
ong></em>, is now in the throes of the MLS season=E2=80=99s business end. S=
ullivan, <em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weig=
ht: 700;">Neil Pierre</strong></em> and Philadelphia struggled to find a rh=
ythm in an opening defeat at New England. Nashville goalkeeper <em><strong =
style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Brian Schwa=
ke</strong></em> shipped an own goal inside 10 minutes, and Nashville never=
 found an equalizer against underdog Cincinnati.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The postseason could also showcase the bes=
t days of a few players who toiled on the outside of the national team duri=
ng Pochettino=E2=80=99s reign. Few strikers of American eligibility have be=
en in as fine form over the past 18 months as <em><strong style=3D"color: #=
0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Milan Iloski</strong></em> (=
age 27), with 31 MLS goals in 3,603 minutes since the start of 2025 , and h=
is scoring touch will be vital in regards to Union=E2=80=99s hopes of swing=
ing their series. FC Dallas center-back <em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6=
; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Nolan Norris</strong></em> (21) fi=
nished a fine first season as a full-time starter with a full-90 in a 3-0 w=
in over Portland. <em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; =
font-weight: 700;">Taha Habroune</strong></em> (20) scored and thrived in t=
he heart of midfield of Columbus=E2=80=99 0-3 dismantling of hosting Inter =
Miami.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Monday night sees St Louis City launch the=
ir MLS Cup hopes with a fantastic domestic double-pivot of <em><strong styl=
e=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Daniel Edelman<=
/strong></em> (23) and <em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: nor=
mal; font-weight: 700;">Chris Durkin</strong></em> (26). On Tuesday, San Jo=
se will hope to make quick work of the Houston Dynamo =E2=80=93 who exist a=
s a relocation of the previous Quakes =E2=80=93 with attacking midfield tec=
hnician <em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weigh=
t: 700;">Niko Tsakiris</strong></em> (21) pulling the strings.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Not the headliners, nor the fading stars o=
f a bygone decade, but the playoffs are MLS at its entertaining best, and t=
here=E2=80=99s still ample reason to watch from a national team perspective=
.</p>
