<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Monday:</strong> Round One of the =
MLS playoffs is in full swing, and it continues on Monday night as one of t=
he league=E2=80=99s more star-studded sides visits the US Open Cup winners.=
 <em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;=
">Los Angeles FC v St Louis City </strong></em>is at 8pm on Apple TV and FS=
1.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Tuesday:</strong> Four games into =
the Champions League, Arsenal are near the top of the table while Borussia =
Dortmund are midway down. The two sides meet in London with Arsenal coming =
off a draw against Newcastle over the weekend.<em><strong style=3D"color: #=
0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;"> Arsenal v Borussia Dortmund=
</strong></em> is at 3pm on Paramount+.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Wednesday: </strong>There=E2=80=99=
s no rest for Manchester United despite their terrible debut under Pochetti=
no over the weekend. The Red Devils must now focus on the Champions League,=
 with a visit to Portugal to play Sporting.<strong> </strong><em><strong st=
yle=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Manchester Un=
ited v Sporting</strong></em> is at 3pm on Paramount+.</p>
